**Cause:** `rstrip` in `more_itertools/more.py:2647-2655` defined `cache_clear` but never called it. So after yielding the cache (a previously-stripped run), the next strip run accumulated on top of the old cache, and the next non-match yielded the whole history again.

**Fix:** call `cache_clear()` right after `yield from cache` in `more_itertools/more.py:2655`. Added a regression test `test_rstrip_no_double_yield` in `tests/test_more.py:3462`.

